    compareNote: 'Red = no; green = yes. A pattern stands out: the parties that took power through their own long wars (China, Vietnam, Cuba, Yugoslavia, North Korea in part) lasted longer than those installed by the Soviet army. Political scientists (Levitsky & Way, Revolution and Dictatorship, 2022) argue that revolutionary origins create unusually cohesive ruling parties and armies.',

